      <activity id="2e86a0b2-2148-508c-8ac2-ec57d7566f0b" activityNameId="b022653f-bf19-56ef-a511-3a0f94d12e0a" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, refractory SPL, Al elec.lysis, 0% water, to residual material landfill</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, refractory SPL, Al elec.lysis, 0% water, to residual material landfill
Inventoried waste contains 100% spent pot liner, refractory fraction; . waste composition (wet, in ppm): H2O n.a.; O 392510; H n.a.; C n.a.; S n.a.; N 330.12; P 80.218; B n.a.; Cl 399.4; Br n.a.; F 85871; I n.a.; Ag n.a.; As n.a.; Ba n.a.; Cd n.a.; Co n.a.; Cr n.a.; Cu n.a.; Hg n.a.; Mn 77.317; Mo n.a.; Ni n.a.; Pb n.a.; Sb n.a.; Se n.a.; Sn n.a.; V n.a.; Zn n.a.; Be n.a.; Sc n.a.; Sr 369.22; Ti 359.16; Tl n.a.; W n.a.; Si 172740; Fe 12568; Ca 39255; Al 195590; K 2486.7; Mg n.a.; Na 97853; Share of carbon in waste that is biogenic 60.4%. Additional solidification with 0.4002 kg of cement.;; UUID: 64732c6b-cb49-4441-8893-7e645095d63f
Waste-specific short-term emissions to water from leachate. Long-term emissions from landfill to ground water. Expenditures for solidificalion with cement (user-specified option)
Location: Technology encountered in Switzerland in 2000. Landfill includes base seal and leachate collection system.
Technology: Swiss residual material landfill for polluted, inorganic waste. With base seal and leachate collection system. Recultivation after closure. 
Time period: Waste composition as given in literature reference, theoretical data or other source. Transfer coefficients from prospective model.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Landfill model based on observed leachate concentrations in literature. Extrapolated to 60'000 years heeding chemical characteristics. Initial waste composition from various literature sources. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: uncertainty of waste input composition data derived from generic formula GSD(c) = N*ln(c)+1. Mean long-term emissions are the emissions until the next glacial period occurs (in 60'000a) and the landfill is eroded. Maximal long-term emissions are the complete emissions of all landfilled material (except Cr). Minimal long-term emissions are derived implicitly from the mean and maximal values assuming a lognormal distribution.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_64732c6b-cb49-4441-8893-7e645095d63f.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
